(project pricklypear-product-experience
 (doc "Pricklypear book chapter: product-experience")
 (status partial)
 (convention ocaml-dune)
 (section product-experience
  (doc "Human-facing product layer: concepts, access paths, legible vocabulary, first-run, horizon")
  (status partial)
  (* agent note (|it32: PARTIAL overall. concepts-guide, vocabulary,
    first-run-recipe implemented; access-paths: browser login now
    in-image (auth.web-login path); horizon planned design-only.
    2026-07-12: product shell layering — environment UI is Lisp;
    OCaml is host/gate/emergency only (see image.system-browser).
    2026-07-12: product theme Path B planned (image.product-theme,
    BORGE-1783837363) — presentation is Lisp css/* sheets, not a
    hard-coded OCaml CSS twin.|) *)
  (verify
   (build "dune build image")
   (smoke "GET /about teaches concepts; home offers first-run hello recipe")
   (smoke "scripts/repl.sh logs into REPL"))
  (details
   (doc (|
        Pricklypear is a multi-user live computing environment:
        log into your image, write Lisp functions stored as data,
        branch code while sharing data, bind functions to URLs,
        let AI propose functions onto a branch.

        Product experience is the thin skin that makes the dense
        substrate legible. Without it, only authors understand
        the system.

        LAYERING (aligned with image.system-browser +
        image.product-theme, 2026-07-12):
        - Environment UI humans live in (nav, home, app menus,
          theme/presentation, user routes) is Lisp on branches
          (libs/*.pp seed + personal pins). That is the product.
        - OCaml hosts Lisp: eval, store, auth gate, health,
          kernel system pages (/bindings, /edit, …), and a
          labeled emergency shell if ui/nav, ui/home, or ui/css
          fails.
        - OCaml must not ship a silent second product nav/home
          or a silent full design-system CSS twin in http.ml.
          Dual silent defaults are rejected architecture.
        - Theme is Path B (honest Lisp): css/* sheets + tokens,
          not CSS-string-in-lambda as the native form.
   |))
  )
  (subsection concepts-guide
   (doc "In-app about page: glossary, access, first tour, horizon summary")
   (status implemented)
   (* agent note (|it32: IMPLEMENTED. GET /about + home link. Markdown
     docs/concepts-and-horizon.md removed; .borg is source of truth.|) *)
   (verify
    (build "dune build image")
    (smoke "GET /about contains Image, Store, Function, Branch, Route, AI"))
   (details
    (doc (|
         GET /about (kernel OCaml page today; may move to Lisp
         later) MUST explain:

         WHAT: multi-user live Lisp environment; image=CPU,
         Postgres=disk; Smalltalk tradition without OOP image dump.

         GLOSSARY:
         - Image: running process (REPL + HTTP); single-image v1
         - Store: Postgres durable truth
         - Function/binding: named live value; define persists
         - Branch: versioned code world; data shared
         - Type/row: deftype + data_rows CRUD
         - Route/page: URL bound to a function
         - Shell (ui/menu, ui/nav, ui/home, ui/theme, ui/css):
           Lisp product chrome + presentation
         - Theme tokens (theme/bg, …): branch-visible style knobs
         - AI propose: agent authors on current branch only

         ACCESS:
         - scripts/dev.sh start (PG + image)
         - Browser: /login (app session) then / /repl /edit /bindings
         - scripts/pp_eval.py or Basic auth for agents
         - scripts/repl.sh / line-protocol REPL when enabled
         - nginx basic-auth may sit at edge; not the user DB

         FIRST TOUR: log in, define hi-page, route /hello, open page,
         edit ui/menu for navbar, optional propose-function.

         Link from home nav and home body. Full horizon detail
         in product-experience.horizon.
    |))
   )
  )
  (subsection access-paths
   (doc "Documented ways humans reach a live image")
   (status partial)
   (* agent note (|2026-07-12: browser password login + session cookie
     ship in-image (auth.web-login / multi-user-product Option B).
     Still partial: edge nginx basic-auth, REPL path, fleet attach.|) *)
   (verify
    (smoke "GET /login form; POST /login mints pp_session")
    (smoke "scripts/verify_auth.sh or auth_product_smoke passes")
    (smoke "scripts/repl.sh connects when line-protocol enabled"))
   (details
    (doc (|
         v1 SHIPPED paths (single-image):
         1. Browser: GET/POST /login → cookie pp_session →
            land on username/personal; POST /logout revokes
         2. Admin: /admin/users (create user, revoke sessions)
         3. Agents: HTTP Basic or session cookie → /api/eval
            (scripts/pp_eval.py)
         4. scripts/dev.sh start — PG + image
         5. scripts/verify_auth.sh product gate
         6. Optional scripts/repl.sh / line-protocol REPL

         Product chrome after login is Lisp (ui/nav, ui/home,
         ui/theme/ui/css). Auth gate and emergency shell/CSS are
         OCaml kernel only.

         DEFERRED:
         - Fleet boot/attach per user (process isolation path)
         - Default real SSH (awa 0.5.x path)
         - Drop nginx htpasswd as primary human gate
           (break-glass only)
    |))
   )
  )
  (subsection vocabulary
   (doc "Friendly UI labels over systems jargon")
   (status implemented)
   (* agent note (|it32: IMPLEMENTED. Nav/home/pages use Functions,
     Pages, Data, Workspace. Lisp prim names unchanged. Smoke checks
     home vocabulary.|) *)
   (verify
    (smoke "nav/home use Functions (not only Bindings) and point to /about"))
   (details
    (doc (|
         UI vocabulary (human):
           Functions  <- function_defs / bindings
           Pages      <- view_bindings / routes
           Data       <- type_defs + data_rows
           Workspace  <- current branch + whoami
           About      <- concepts guide

         HARD RULE: Page ≠ Function.
           Page = URL endpoint (/hello). Function = named code (hi-page).
           Edit targets are always function names (/edit/hi-page).
           Page inspect is /page/hello (route + call graph).
           Never nav-link /edit/<route-basename> as if it were a function.

         PACKAGE vs BRANCH:
           Package = in-branch prefix (todo/) for organizing functions.
           Branch = versioned workspace (system/main).
           UI labels: "package" for prefixes, "branch"/"workspace" for
           version worlds — never swap the words.
           Functions browser groups by package; branch chrome stays
           whoami + current branch.

         Lisp/REPL vocabulary stays technical (define, route,
         deftype, rows). The browser skin translates.
    |))
   )
  )
  (subsection first-run-recipe
   (doc "One-click or one-form 'make a hello page' onboarding")
   (status implemented)
   (* agent note (|it32: IMPLEMENTED. POST /api/recipe/hello + home
     button create hi-page + /hello route. Smoke: GET /hello works.|) *)
   (verify
    (build "dune build image")
    (smoke "POST /api/recipe/hello creates hi-page route; GET /hello works"))
   (details
    (doc (|
         Recipe "hello page":
         1. Define function hi-page -> render-html greeting
         2. (route "/hello" "hi-page")
         3. Return link to /hello and /edit/hi-page

         Exposed as:
         - Button/form on home
         - POST /api/recipe/hello

         Non-goals: full app wizard (that's AI app-sketch later).
    |))
   )
  )
  (subsection horizon
   (doc "Long-term possible futures built on this substrate (design only)")
   (status planned)
   (* agent note (|it32: design-only. Migrated from
     docs/concepts-and-horizon.md. Not an implementation checklist;
     guides prioritization and pitching.|) *)
   (details
    (doc (|
         Possible futures (not commitments):

         A. Personal computing environment
            Always-on personal image; notes/CRM/automations
            as live functions; browser as desktop.

         B. Multi-user community OS
            system/main commons; personal garden branches;
            merge reviews; author-runs-as-author capabilities.

         C. AI-native software workshop
            AI cohabits image; proposes types+fns+routes as
            app sketches; binding-level diffs; provenance;
            later addressable AST patches.

         D. Internal tools platform
            Team branches; shared business objects; live
            inspectable tools without redeploy for Lisp-tier
            changes.

         E. Education / research lab
            Legible multi-user systems + PL teaching with
            forks/merges and visible isolation.

         F. End-user programmable products
            Friendly skin on same substrate; templates as
            starter branches; AI drafts, users edit.

         G. Hardened multi-tenant service
            Solo5, real SSH + web login, argon2, mTLS,
            fleet policies, true setuid data scoping.

         H. Dabar — live Bible study libraries
            BSB reader + Strong's + interlinear as load-library
            packages (bible/ + dabar/) on the image; not a
            separate OS. Spec: dabar.borg (root-inlined chapter).
            Semantic search deferred.

         Milestone ladder:
           now   — hacker env + browser login + Lisp product shell
                   (define/edit/route/AI; ui/nav ui/home; auth session)
           next  — product theme Path B (css/* + ui/theme); kill
                   silent OCaml product defaults (nav/home/CSS);
                   emergency-only chrome+css; shell denser; branch
                   promote UI
           later — environment feel (more system UI in Lisp,
                   permissions, multi-user fleet isolation)
           horizon — community + AI coworker + Solo5 product

         Branch UX + software updates: see branching.borg
         subsections personal-workspace (implemented),
         package-updates / promote / branch-browser-ui
         (planned). Defaults on system/main; garden on
         <user>/personal; promote is selective merge + git.

         Principles to preserve:
           live system over file tree; store is truth;
           code branches / data shared; functions compose;
           AI is an author not god mode; inspectability;
           isolation by process.
    |))
   )
  )
 )
)
